 "text": "Skip to main content\nHome\nGovernment\nBoards & Committees\nCounty Board\nKittson County Extension Committee\nKittson County Township / City Officers\nAgendas & Minutes\nCounty Finances\nBudgets\nFinancial Statements\nTruth in Taxation\nOrdinances\nImportant Documents\nDepartments\nAssessors\nCounty Administrator\nCourt Administration\nDriver's License & Motor Vehicle\nElections\nEmergency Management\nEnvironmental Services\nFinancial Service\nHighway Department\nInformation Technology\nRecorder\nSheriff\nSocial Services\nTaxpayer Services\nVeteran Services\nZoning\nCommunity\nUniversity of Minnesota Extension\nKittson County SWCD\nTwo Rivers Watershed District\nKittson County Trailblazers\nKittson County Veterans Memorial\nMemorial Pics\nGIS\nCommunity Events\nHow Do I?\nApply For\nPassports\nAdult Services\nChild Support Services\nChildcare Assistance Program\nChildren's Services\nDriver's License & Motor Vehicle\nEmployment Opportunities\nFinancial Assistance / Food Support\nHomestead Credit\nMedical Programs\nVeteran Services\nContact\nDepartment Personnel\nSubmit\nA Concern\nAssessment Valuation / Classification Appeal\nProperty Tax Payment\nSearch\nGo\nstart animation start slide 1 of 1\nRecorder\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments\nRecorder\nRecorder\nThe County Recorder is the custodian of all legal records pertaining to real estate, birth, death, marriage, marriage credentials, notary public, and tax liens.\nWhen acting as the Registrar of Titles, the County Recorder reviews each document before recording to determine if the document will cloud the title, similar to when an attorney examines ab abstract for abstract property. When property is held in a trust, estate or is part of court proceeding, the Examiner of Titles issues a Directive to the Registrar of Title regarding how to proceed.\nRecorder’s Mission Statement\nTo protect, preserve and record documents relating to real estate, vital statistics in a methodical manner for posterity in legal and security purposes. To serve the public in a prompt, courteous and effective manner.\nMarriage License Application\nMarriage Licenses\nComplete and submit your Marriage License Application online . Choose Submit Application on MOMS website.\nOnce the Marriage License Application has been submitted, a marriage license may be issued in any county in Minnesota and may be used in any county in Minnesota. The record of marriage will only be on file in the county in which the application was issued.\nTo obtain a marriage license from Kittson County, both applicants should appear in person, Monday through Friday between 8 am to 4 pm. If applicable, also bring in your Statement of Premarital Education (PDF) . If one of the parties cannot appear in person, a Supplemental Marriage License Application will be given to the party appearing before us to be completed by the non-appearing marriage applicant. The license must be used within six months from the date of issuance.\nWe only accept cash or check for the following fees that would apply:\nIssuance of Marriage License: $125.00\nIssuance of Marriage License with a Statement of Premarital Education: $50.00\nFees are non-refundable.\n|\nRecorder\nPhone: 218-843-2842\nOffice Hours: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m.\nKristen Hultgren\nKittson County Recorder\nShannon Bakken\nDeputy Recorder\n|\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nAfrikaans\nAlbanian\nArabic\nArmenian\nAzerbaijani\nBasque\nBelarusian\nBengali\nBosnian\nBulgarian\nCatalan\nCebuano\nChinese (Simplified)\nChinese (Traditional)\nCroatian\nCzech\nDanish\nDutch\nEnglish\nEsperanto\nEstonian\nFilipino\nFinnish\nFrench\nGalician\nGeorgian\nGerman\nGreek\nGujarati\nHaitian Creole\nHausa\nHebrew\nHindi\nHmong\nHungarian\nIcelandic\nIgbo\nIndonesian\nIrish\nItalian\nJapanese\nJavanese\nKannada\nKhmer\nKorean\nLao\nLatin\nLatvian\nLithuanian\nMacedonian\nMalay\nMaltese\nMaori\nMarathi\nMongolian\nNepali\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nPunjabi\nRomanian\nRussian\nSerbian\nSlovak\nSlovenian\nSoma